    "text": "So why doesn't Russia just make its own? Because it can't. Russia's most advanced chip factory, Mikron, just outside Moscow, works with technology roughly two decades behind the cutting edge. The world's best chips are designed in America, manufactured in Taiwan and South Korea, and built with machines from the Netherlands and Japan. Russia sits outside that entire chain. It can build the missile, it can't build the brain.",
